      "file": "fleet_telemetry/models.py",
      "line_hint": "59",
      "evidence": "+    covariance: tuple[tuple[float, ...], ...] = ((0.0,) * 6,) * 6  # 6x6 pose covariance, row-major\n+    health: float = 1.0  # composite localisation/drive health, 0..1",
      "explanation": "DriftSpec adds covariance and health as required fields, but TelemetryFrame gives them defaults (zero 6x6 matrix and 1.0). Direct construction can omit them silently and pass shape check, hiding incomplete migration; the zero covariance is singular and would fail fusion with inv(). Required wire fields should be required in the domain model.",
      "suggested_fix": "Make covariance and health required without defaults (or use field with no default / dataclass KW_ONLY). Keep _check_covariance_shape validation and let missing health raise TypeError; client already raises TelemetryParseError for missing wire fields."
    },
    {
      "severity": "low",
      "category": "incomplete_migration",
      "file": "fleet_telemetry/client.py",
      "line_hint": "32",
      "evidence": "+        health = float(payload[\"health\"])",
      "explanation": "Spec defines health as 0..1 required. Client parses and stores it but never validates the range, so out-of-range values (e.g., 1.5, -0.2) are accepted silently. Alerts only check <0.5.",
      "suggested_fix": "Validate 0.0 <= health <= 1.0 after float conversion and raise TelemetryParseError if outside, matching the noise >0 validation."
    }
  ]
}
